Sometimes I forget how crazy the internet actually is.

If I want to learn something today, I can find a 2-hour course, a 10-minute YouTube video, documentation, a GitHub repository, a Reddit thread from someone who had the exact same problem, or an AI that can explain it to me.

And most of it is free.

It's probably never been easier to teach yourself something.

The difficult part isn't finding information anymore.

It's deciding what information is actually worth your time.

